Q: Calling model method with $this-&gt;example_model()-&gt;methodName() emits &quot;Fatal error: Call to undefined method&quot; A: <p>Simply load your model inside the constructor</p>

<pre><code>public function __construct()
{
    parent::__construct();
    $this-&gt;load-&gt;model('users_model');
}
</code></pre>

<p>Then simply call the relevant functions inside any controller functions like this.</p>

<pre><code>public function index()
{

$data = '';

$data['testing'] =  $this-&gt; users_model-&gt; test_user();

$this-&gt;load-&gt;view('home',$data);
}
</code></pre>
